 quest involving a cursed creature and a  house full of spoons it's been a day  since I completed that quest yet I'm  still thinking about the truth I found  there and the punishment its primary  character endured was it rightful  punishment I'm not sure but I've spent a  good time contemplating whether my good  choice was well and truly good and shall  sit and dine with you at your table no  spoon you have shall say to you never  again shall you wish to spy your  reflection in the mirror I do miss the  old gang however blood and wine has a  dearth of sorceresses and Dwarfs though  no shortage of horrific creatures to  slay and certainly no shortage of quests  to take things can get a bit repetitive  a few dally on one quest line for too  long solving the problems of a couple of  vineyards becomes a boring cycle of  fighting the same monsters in different  areas  luckily even the rare on exciting quests  can yield welcome rewards one of which  is the DTR own upgradeable vineyard in a  state don't expect fallout 4 levels of  customization blood and wine is more  similar to Far Cry primal in this regard  presenting a series of automated  improvements that cost a certain amount  of cash blood and wine also introduces a  supplementary mutation system as a quest  reward for a melancholy storyline it's a  smart mechanic opening up new  possibilities once you've no reason to  spend skill points on upgrades you  either won't use or have no slot for  you'll certainly be glad for the passive  improvements during the tougher  encounters which are much more taxing  than before  sometimes exhaustively so be prepared to  rethink your strategy when living  statues pepper the ground with magical  traps or when giant centipedes rise from  the earth to surround you and don't  forget to save from time-to-time blood  and wines checkpoints don't always work  in your favor  blood and wine is outrageously beautiful  it's new region Tucson takes the air of  the French countryside though its skies  are bluer its foliage is more lush and  its rolling hills are more impressive  it's as close to high fantasy this dark  fantasy series has gotten and it's all  the better for it it says if the witcher  two's elven rose garden had been  expanded to continental proportions  every rose has its thorns however dank  caves Harbor terrible beasts and  cemeteries shelter the most horrid of  two songs residents the creepiest  accordion tunes you've ever heard SERP 2  underlined the horror it's not a  surprise given the witcher 3 is  consistently excellent audio  notwithstanding a few too many glitches  where Geralt speaks over himself when  you activate multiple triggers at once  nice tune indeed there's more to say  about the witcher 3 blood and wine of  course and i'll have a full review for  you once i finished for now however i  can confirm what you likely guessed  blood and wine is quite good quite big  and quite likely to make you glad to  return to one of videogames most  engaging worlds damn it  you
 

